WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:11.626
In the Encyclopedia of Triangle Centers, the Incentral Triangle I a I b I c and the Excentral Triangle J a J b J c are the cevian and anticevian triangles of the Incenter X one.

2
00:00:11.626 --> 00:00:17.450
Their six vertices are the harmonic bisector feet and the three excenters of triangle A B C.

3
00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:30.640
Because the interior and exterior angle bisectors at each vertex A, B, and C are strictly perpendicular, the vertices A, B, C are the altitude feet of the excentral triangle, and the Incenter X one is the orthocenter of the excentral triangle!

4
00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:39.991
This makes reference triangle A B C the orthic triangle of its own excentral triangle, and the circumcircle of A B C is the nine-point circle of the excentral triangle.

5
00:00:39.991 --> 00:00:47.540
Meanwhile, connecting the excenters through the side midpoints produces the Mittenpunkt X nine, the symmedian point of the excentral triangle.
